<h2>How it is built</h2>
<pre><code>Pointer events (browser)
  -> batched once per animation frame
  -> StrokeBuilder      spacing filter, streamline smoothing, pressure
  -> Stroke + Brush     immutable vector model
  -> DrawingOperation   the unit of undo, diffing and collaboration
  -> InkDocument        layers of elements
  -> IRenderContext     canvas commands, SVG, or the built-in rasterizer</code></pre>

<p>
    One rendering path serves the screen, SVG export and PNG export, so the exported file always matches what
    was drawn. Pointer input never triggers a Blazor render: samples arrive once per frame, the active tool
    processes them, and only the affected canvas layer is redrawn.
</p>

<div class="note">
    In WebAssembly the command buffer reaches JavaScript as a view over managed memory, so a redraw costs one
    interop call and no serialization. In Blazor Server the same engine runs on the server and a lightweight
    trail is drawn locally while each batch is in flight, so the pen still feels attached to the hand.
</div>

@code {
    private InkCanvas? _canvas;
    private readonly Brush _brush = new PenBrush { Width = 4f, Color = InkColor.Parse("#111827") };

    private void Undo() => _canvas?.Undo();

    private void Clear() => _canvas?.Clear();
}
